Let the targets that must be archives be archives

Mesa says shared_library for everything a program links to draw through it:
the gallium target, which is where every gallium driver ends up, EGL, which
links that target, and each Vulkan driver, which is the driver itself. Those
are written as shared_library rather than library, so -Ddefault_library
does not reach them and the build makes shared objects whatever it was
asked for.

A program that cannot open a shared object needs all of them as archives.
library() is Meson's spelling of "whatever this build was asked for", which
is what the rest of Mesa already uses -- and the comment at the top of the
gallium target says the static target is the one this build system was
converted from.

